1/9783991061632.pdf","formatType":"pdf"},{"url":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/118140/2/9783991061632.pdf.txt","formatType":"txt"}],"lastModified":"2026-10-20","summary":"Reinhard Meßner’s 65th birthday provides the occasion to explore, in a commemorative volume, a subject area of relevance to both religious studies and theology, to which the honouree has recently devoted particular attention: Cult – Magic – Ritual. The authors of this volume base their contributions on key themes in Reinhard Meßner’s work. They are all connected to him in their own way: as colleagues in the field of Catholic liturgical studies, as discussion partners in historical, philological and religious studies disciplines, and as personal companions.","coverUrl":"https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/20.500.12657/118140/3/9783991061632.pdf.jpg"}